# MON Unlock Widget — Core Conventions

This project builds a paste-anywhere paywall: `<mon-unlock>` custom element. Readers pay native **MON** on **Monad mainnet (chain 143)** to unlock the full article body. Publishers copy one HTML block; no accounts, no backend required from them.

## Guiding Principles
- Phase 1 (shipped): real on-chain MON payment + cross-device unlock verification.
- Publisher UX: one embed snippet. Body lives in Supabase, not in the HTML.
- Identity = wallet address. No email/password accounts.
- On-chain is the source of truth for unlocks; local cache is a performance convenience.
- Keep the embed contract stable. Changes to the generated HTML must be intentional and versioned.

## Repository Layout
- `src/core/` — pure business logic (no DOM). Types, unlock services, wallet manager, chains.
- `src/widget/` — Lit custom element + component CSS. The `<mon-unlock>` implementation.
- `src/index.ts` — library entry; re-exports and side-effect import of the custom element.
- `*.html` (root) — static single-file apps: generator, dashboard, register, embed-example, index. They duplicate some constants because they must run without bundling.
- `supabase/functions/*/index.ts` — Deno Edge Functions (CORS, service role for writes).
- `contracts/src/` — Foundry Solidity (`ArticleUnlock.sol`).
- `skills/mon-unlock-embed/` — OpenClaw plugin that re-uses the embed generation and Supabase sync logic. Must match generator output exactly.
- `dist/` — build output (do not edit). Produced by `npm run build`.

## TypeScript / Module Rules
- Target: ES2022, ESM output. `"moduleResolution": "bundler"`.
- **Always import relative files with `.js` extension** from `.ts` sources:
  ```ts
  import { monadMainnet } from "./chains.js";
  import type { WalletState } from "./types.js";
  ```
- Bare specifiers stay bare: `"lit"`, `"viem"`, `"@walletconnect/ethereum-provider"`.
- Re-export via barrels (`src/core/index.ts`).
- Strict mode; no implicit any.

## Widget (Lit) Conventions
- Custom element: `@customElement("mon-unlock") export class MonUnlock extends LitElement`.
- Light DOM: `createRenderRoot() { return this; }`. Styles come from `dist/mon-unlock.css` + host page.
- Slots are the contract with publishers:
  - `slot="teaser"` — always visible (plain text or simple HTML).
  - `slot="body"` — shown only after unlock (optional; fetched from Supabase if absent).
- Body content handling:
  - If it contains HTML tags (`<p`, `<br`, etc.), render via `unsafeHTML`.
  - Otherwise, treat as plain text and render with `whitespace-pre-wrap` so blank lines and indentation become paragraphs.
- Two runtime modes (determined by presence of `unlock-contract` attribute):
  - Demo: `UnlockService` + localStorage (no chain).
  - On-chain: `OnchainUnlockService` + viem calls against the provided contract.
- Pre-flight: before sending an on-chain unlock, call `getArticle` to surface clear errors (not registered, inactive) instead of letting MetaMask warn "tx will fail".
- Use explicit `gas` on writes when Monad RPC estimation is unreliable.
- Events: `mon:unlocked`, `mon:connected` (bubbles, composed).
- Teaser in the locked state uses a styled box; after unlock it is plain text above the body.

## On-Chain Model (Non-Negotiable)
- Chain: Monad mainnet (id 143). `monadMainnet` in `src/core/chains.ts`.
- Payment: native MON only (`payable unlock`, `msg.value` in wei). No USDC or custom tokens in v1.
- Article ID encoding (must be identical everywhere):
  ```ts
  const articleIdBytes = keccak256(toBytes(slug)); // viem
  // Solidity: keccak256(bytes(slug))
  ```
- Contract functions used by widget: `unlock(bytes32)`, `hasUnlocked(address,bytes32)`, `getArticle(bytes32)`, `registerArticle(bytes32,uint256)`.
- Canonical contract (mainnet): `0x038446b1F736e254cC0E256B20D74823c41EeADB`.
- Overpayment is forwarded (no refund in MVP).
- One unlock per (reader, article). Re-unlock reverts with `AlreadyUnlocked`.

## Dual Source of Truth for Unlocks
- Local cache (`UnlockStore` / `localStorage`) makes UI instant and survives refreshes.
- `checkOnchainAccess` (or on-chain `hasUnlocked`) is authoritative.
- After a successful on-chain payment or a positive on-chain check, write to cache.
- Silent discovery (`eth_accounts`) on load when `unlock-contract` is present enables cross-origin "already paid" without re-clicking connect.
- First visit on a new origin typically still requires one explicit connect; subsequent visits on that origin can auto-detect.

## Supabase / Edge Functions
- All functions: `Deno.serve(async (req) => { ... })`.
- Standard CORS headers object (vary by method). Always handle OPTIONS.
- Writes use `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`.
- `register-article`: upsert by `article_id_hash`. Stores human slug + body + teaser so the dashboard and `article-body` can serve the exact embed later.
- `article-body`: returns body only if the reader has an unlock row or on-chain `hasUnlocked` is true. Falls back to on-chain truth for immediate post-payment UX.
- `indexer`: cron-driven; paginates `getLogs` for `ArticleRegistered` / `ArticleUnlocked`, upserts into `articles`/`unlocks`, tracks `indexer_state.last_indexed_block`.
- `backfill-unlock`: dev helper only; not public.
- Schema drift note: indexer may write rows with `article_id = null`; `article-body` backfills the slug when possible.

## Content Model
- `teaser`: free preview. Supports newlines via `whitespace-pre-wrap` in the widget. Escaped when emitted into embed HTML.
- `body`: paid content. Either plain text (newlines → paragraphs) or HTML (rendered). Never put the body in the pasted embed HTML; it is fetched after unlock.
- Price: human string in generator ("1", "0.5"); stored in wei on chain and in Supabase.

## Constants and Duplication (Keep in Sync)
These values are intentionally duplicated across static pages and the skills plugin because those artifacts must be self-contained:
- `CDN_BASE`: `https://mon-unlock-widget-production.up.railway.app`
- `MAINNET_CONTRACT`: `0x038446b1F736e254cC0E256B20D74823c41EeADB`
- `WIDGET_VERSION`: bump when widget behavior or embed shape changes (affects cache-busting `?v=` in script src).
- `WC_PROJECT_ID`: `c2a289e11ad2998f8ea4633db536334c`
- `MONAD_RPC`: `https://rpc.monad.xyz`

When any of the above change, update **all** of:
- `generator.html`
- `dashboard.html`
- `register.html`
- `skills/mon-unlock-embed/embed.ts`
- (and any docs/examples that hardcode them)

## Embed Generation Contract
- `generator.html` produces the canonical embed HTML.
- `skills/mon-unlock-embed/embed.ts` `generateEmbed` and `publishArticle` must emit **identical** markup and use the same constants.
- The teaser slot content is HTML-escaped in the generated code.
- The body is **never** in the generated snippet; it is synced to Supabase and fetched post-unlock.

## Error and UX Tone
- Errors shown to end users must be actionable sentences, not stack traces or internal codes.
- Examples: "This article has not been registered for on-chain payments yet.", "Install a Web3 wallet or provide a WalletConnect project ID for mobile."
- Pre-flight checks surface the right message before MetaMask shows a scary warning.
- WalletConnect on mobile has custom QR + visibility/poll recovery because iOS often approves in the wallet app while the page tab is backgrounded.

## Comment Style
- Prefer JSDoc for public or cross-module functions and classes.
- Write "why" comments, not "what the next line does."
- Avoid obvious narrative comments inside function bodies (e.g., do not write `// set the state` before `this.state = ...`).
- Contract and edge functions may have short header blocks explaining purpose and verification order.

## Build, Dev, and Tooling
- `npm run dev` — Vite dev server (serves root; widget served from `/dist` after build or via plugin).
- `npm run build` — `tsc && vite build --mode lib` (outputs `dist/mon-unlock.js`, `.css`, `.umd.cjs`).
- `npm run typecheck` — `tsc --noEmit`.
- Node >= 22.
- Tailwind via Vite plugin (`@tailwindcss/vite`).
- No ESLint/Prettier enforced in repo at time of writing; follow existing formatting and the patterns in `src/`.
- Contracts: Foundry. `cd contracts && forge test`. Deploy via `forge script`.

## What the Widget Does NOT Do
- It does not host or inline the paid body in the embed HTML.
- It does not create publisher accounts; wallet address is identity.
- It does not support custom tokens or dynamic pricing in v1 (see FOCUS.md for gated items).

## Navigation Header (Static Pages)
All root HTML pages include a minimal inline nav with active-state highlighting via a small IIFE. Keep the three links consistent:
- Home (`/`)
- Create embed (`/generator.html`)
- Writer dashboard (`/dashboard.html`)

## Skills Plugin Specifics
- `skills/mon-unlock-embed/embed.ts` is the single source for the plugin's embed + Supabase + on-chain registration behavior.
- It must stay byte-compatible with what the web generator emits for the same inputs.
- When `privateKey` is provided, the plugin can register on-chain automatically. Otherwise it produces a `finishRegistrationUrl` pointing at `/register.html?slug=...&price=...`.

## Testing and Verification Patterns
- Contract tests (Foundry) assert the core invariants: payment forwarding, insufficient payment revert, double-unlock revert, and `articleIdFromString` matches `keccak256(bytes(slug))`.
- Widget behavior is primarily verified manually via the generator preview + `/demo.html` (or equivalent) with real MON on the target network.
- Cross-device unlock: pay on one browser, connect the same wallet on another origin; `hasUnlocked` + silent `eth_accounts` should surface the body without a second payment.

## When Changing Behavior
- If the embed HTML shape or widget attribute contract changes, bump `WIDGET_VERSION` and update all constant locations.
- If on-chain semantics change (events, function signatures), update the ABI fragments in the widget, generator, register page, dashboard, and skills plugin.
- Document the change in FOCUS.md or a new note if it affects Phase exit criteria or trust assumptions.

## Out of Scope (Per FOCUS.md)
Do not pursue without explicit validation:
- IPFS / decentralized storage for bodies
- USDC or other payment assets in v1
- Custom `$READ` token or usage-based pricing before talking to credible Monad/DeltaV contacts
- WordPress/Webflow plugins before the hosted generator (Phase 2) is solid

Follow FOCUS.md as the source of truth for what to build next and what to ignore.

---

Follow these rules so that any change—widget, generator, contract, or plugin—remains consistent with the existing mental model and the paste-anywhere promise.